From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:55:19 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Stop using octoprint.util.comm (broken on OctoPrint 2.0)

OctoPrint 2.0.0 moved the comm layer into the bundled serial_connector
plugin. octoprint.util.comm is now only a deprecated re-export shim that
the core no longer imports, so `octoprint.util.comm.gcode_command_for_cmd`
fails with:

    AttributeError: module 'octoprint.util' has no attribute 'comm'

ThumbnailService and HelperFileService only used it to find the first
extrusion move. Replace that with a local `is_extrusion_move()` helper
with the same semantics, so the plugin no longer depends on OctoPrint
internals for it.

Add tests that pin the expected behaviour and, when OctoPrint is
installed, compare it against OctoPrint's original implementation.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T9yYaTfwp21kvTkb3Tj7fp
